Based on the recorded evidence, the fact-check confirms that a viral message claiming "all Haldiram’s food products were banned in USA" was widely circulated, as referenced by a fact-check article published on September 3, 2020, which explicitly labels it as a "viral message" and addresses its spread. While the evidence also shows that no comprehensive ban existed (with products remaining available and only specific batches facing import refusals), the claim's content is specifically about the existence of this viral message, not the veracity of its content.

The evidence is clear and sufficient to verify the central claim that such a message gained traction. No further investigation is needed regarding the message's virality, as it is directly documented.

