A viral message claiming a blanket U.S. ban on all Haldiram’s products was documented and fact-checked as spreading widely, notably in an [article from September 3, 2020](https://newsmeter.in/fact-check-viral-message-that-all-haldirams-food-products-were-banned-in-usa-is-false/). The investigation found no comprehensive ban was ever issued; only [specific batches were refused entry](https://www.financialexpress.com/business/industry-after-lead-in-maggi-itspesticides-in-haldirams-86628/) due to contamination, and products remained [available for sale](https://www.just-food.com/news/indian-snacks-group-haldirams-in-us-push/). Therefore, the fact-check confirms the *existence and spread* of the viral message, even though its content was false.